      "vision_reason": "The museum's own description explicitly attributes these blowpipe darts/arrows to the Dayak of Borneo, only speculating that the poison name \"Upos\" may derive from the Javanese word \"Upas\" — this is a linguistic aside, not evidence the objects are Javanese-made. The record's claimed ethnicity does not match the culture documented in the metadata.",
