        "image": "good",
        "era": "traditional",
        "reason": "The image shows three poisoned blowpipe darts/arrows with bamboo shafts, pith stoppers, and pointed tips, matching the museum's description of Dayak blowpipe darts used with poison (\"Upas\"). This is a weapon type documented as made and used by Dayak peoples of Borneo."
